2. What&#x27;s going on with CoreWeave
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet; Chart: Matt Phillips/Axios CoreWeave shares surged today after a second-quarter earnings report that seemed to tickle the market's fancy, Axios' Matt Phillips writes. 

 Why it matters: As a neocloud — a company that builds data centers and sells AI compute — CoreWeave can say a lot about both the unit economics of AI and the market vibe on the technology.

 📊 The latest: Demand seemed strong.

 Sales more than doubled, to $2.58 billion. Remaining performance obligations — a measure of sales backlog — jumped 245%, to $103.7 billion. 📉 Yes, but: The company's expenses are growing too — along with its losses.

 Its adjusted net loss worsened to $567 million from $130 million during the same quarter last year. 👋 The intrigue: It's likely the gangbusters stock move after the earnings report — it jumped 19% — had something to do with the large short position embedded in CoreWeave.

 Recent data showed more than 20% of its float was in the hands of shorts, who must repurchase shares to exit their trades, a technical feature that can cause a sudden run-up in share prices, known as a short squeeze, when shorts exit a trade en masse. 
 
 
